WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.930
Have you been considering pulling the trigger
on that million-dollar business idea?

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.530
You’ve got a killer product and genius marketing
plan.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.080
But what about the finances, legal, and tax
stuff?

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.860
LLC’s, Partnerships, DBA’s, S Corp...ahhh!!

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.720
The sad truth is, too many people put off
implementing a good idea in the proper way

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.180
because they’re intimidated.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.950
But fear not -- we’ve got you covered.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.360
And it’s probably not as complicated or
as costly as you might think.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:33.220
So let’s get our Business Building Blocks
out and see what goes into building a business

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.420
the right way.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:48.540
The first step is to put on your CFO hat and
get to work setting up your finances correctly.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.800
Do you need to set up a business bank account?

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.700
Or is a personal checking okay if you’re
just starting out?

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.220
Experts agree that the most important thing
is to separate your business money from your

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.160
personal money.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:00:59.880
Completely.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.160
No leaks!

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.320
It will help you avoid bookkeeping and tax
headaches before they start.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.420
And when you’re just starting out, using
a separate personal checking account can be

00:01:08.429 --> 00:01:13.579
fine, but eventually, upgrading to a BUSINESS
checking account can offer special benefits

00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:18.179
-- like additional protection of your personal
assets if things go south.

00:01:18.179 --> 00:01:23.090
All your initial set up costs like a website
or logo-design should come from this account

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.859
and not your personal one.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:30.460
It will also eventually be the destination
for income once those benjamins start rolling in.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.120
Now it’s time to decide on a legal structure.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:40.100
If your business is on the smaller side, you’ve
got some simpler options, like the Sole Proprietorship.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:46.160
A “sole proprietor” business has one owner,
you, and is not a separate entity under the law.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.220
If this is your choice, you won’t have to
file anything with the government to get started

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:55.749
But you may be personally held responsible
for any debts the business might incur.

00:01:55.749 --> 00:02:00.770
And come tax time, all the profit or loss
from that business will run through your personal

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.509
tax return.

00:02:02.509 --> 00:02:06.719
You can operate the business under your own
personal name, or you can choose to use a

00:02:06.719 --> 00:02:09.579
DBA or “doing business as”.

00:02:09.579 --> 00:02:14.540
For instance, when I had a professional organizing
business, I wanted my clients to be able to

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:18.870
make checks out to “Swiss Miss Organizing,”
rather than my name.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.319
It just felt more professional.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:24.900
But before I could get a business account
called “Swiss Miss Organizing,” I had

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.040
to file a DBA for that name.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.930
This is done at the county level, and most
counties allow for a pretty easy online filing

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.069
process.

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:37.329
There will most likely be filing fees, but
it’s usually under a hundred bucks.

00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:41.650
If you decide to share ownership of a business
with at least one other person, then you’ll

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.819
need to form a partnership.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:48.280
It might be worth it to hire a small business
attorney to help you draft up an agreement.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:52.760
The money you spend will be WELL worth it
to have clarity of ownership and operating

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:53.970
agreements.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:59.780
Small business partnerships implode all the
time due to vague or non-existant contracting.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:05.440
Partnerships require not only a DBA but also
an Electronic Identification Number, easily

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.780
obtained from the IRS website.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.820
This acts like a social security number for
your business and will allow you to file a

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.209
tax return for the business itself.

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:17.670
BUT the business doesn’t pay income tax.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:22.890
Instead, it "passes through" any profits or
losses to its partners, meaning the partners

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:26.890
are personally on the hook for any taxes…
or legal troubles.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:31.579
If that sounds scary, you might want to consider
a Limited Liability Company.

00:03:31.579 --> 00:03:37.329
The LLC shields the partners from most legal
responsibility and protects their personal

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:40.840
assets should a client sue the business for
some reason.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.540
Putting an LLC in place can cost a few hundred
to a few thousand dollars, depending on your

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.890
state and whether you hire a professional
to help you.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:53.139
That can increase the cost a bit, but it’s
better than finding out too late that you’re

00:03:53.139 --> 00:03:55.830
not protected because it was improperly set
up.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:04:00.040
Keep in mind that the advantages here are
for legal protection only.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.510
LLC’s don’t change how the partners are
taxed.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:08.180
For that, you need to go one more step up:
a corporation.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:13.400
The most common type for small business owners
is the Subchapter S-Corporation.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:17.230
Unlike all the other arrangements we’ve
talked about, an S-Corp is considered by the

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:22.920
government to be its own discrete entity,
both for legal AND tax-related purposes.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:27.620
Instead of just absorbing the profits (or
losses), your business now PAYS YOU as an

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.620
employee and/or owner.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:34.000
And because this income is taxed at a different
rate, it can mean some real savings.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.330
But there are costs associated with filing
for an S-Corp, and they can get pretty hefty.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:44.170
There’s filing charges, an additional tax
return you’ll have to get prepared, and

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:47.650
likely ongoing charges for a payroll service.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:51.940
It all may be worth it for the tax saving
you get… or not.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:57.110
To know for sure, you should speak with a
tax specialist… which brings us to our final

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.160
building block!

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.660
Get some experts in your corner.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:05.340
Any small business owner will tell you that
when it comes to laws and taxes, one simple

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.760
mistake can lead to massive headaches down
the road.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:13.060
Selecting the right business entity is just
one of the many critical decisions they can

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.110
help you with.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:18.170
When you’re just starting out, we really
recommend building a relationship with a good

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.820
CPA, bookkeeper, and small business attorney.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:26.100
It’s their job to help you make smart decisions…
while still playing by the rules.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.000
Building a small business might feel daunting
at first.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.880
But if you take your time, do your research,
and set things up right from day one, you’ll

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.280
be reaching your dreams before you know it.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.820
And that’s our two cents!

